1
00:00:01,417 --> 00:00:04,999
It's been years.
I'm just not very good with people.

2
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:08,416
Accessing previous files
relating to program VisionQuest.

3
00:00:08,417 --> 00:00:09,832
Welcome home, Vision.

4
00:00:09,833 --> 00:00:11,249
So, you were smiling today,

5
00:00:11,250 --> 00:00:12,250
- which is good.
- Mmm-hmm.

6
00:00:13,417 --> 00:00:14,666
Miss Edith.

7
00:00:14,667 --> 00:00:18,416
This house is architecturally
and emotionally unstable.

8
00:00:18,417 --> 00:00:20,457
Well, he knows
the facts of his old life.

9
00:00:20,458 --> 00:00:22,249
Now, he's searching for the feeling of it.

10
00:00:22,250 --> 00:00:25,166
You're a ghost, haunting her footsteps.

11
00:00:25,167 --> 00:00:26,832
Not her footsteps, his.

12
00:00:26,833 --> 00:00:29,749
I wish to understand him
and how he existed in this world.

13
00:00:29,750 --> 00:00:32,707
You're familiar with the thought
experiment the Ship of Theseus?

14
00:00:32,708 --> 00:00:35,208
- Naturally.
- When no original plank remains,

15
00:00:35,917 --> 00:00:37,833
is it still the Ship of Theseus?

16
00:00:40,292 --> 00:00:41,999
Both are the true ship.

17
00:00:42,000 --> 00:00:47,542
Someone out there placed a sizeable bounty
on Vision's AI-infested head.

18
00:00:48,875 --> 00:00:51,166
Hey V, skylight exit?

19
00:00:51,167 --> 00:00:53,041
And the contract
went to a hunter,

20
00:00:53,042 --> 00:00:55,000
known only as "the Paladin".

21
00:00:56,000 --> 00:00:57,999
-  What do you got?
- He has a family.

22
00:00:58,000 --> 00:01:02,457
Had. Twin boys, Billy and Tommy.

23
00:01:02,458 --> 00:01:04,166
Thought deceased for years

24
00:01:04,167 --> 00:01:07,332
The Vision has suddenly
and violently reappeared.

25
00:01:07,333 --> 00:01:08,416
You're right.

26
00:01:08,417 --> 00:01:10,707
- You're name's Thomas Shepherd.
- Is it?

27
00:01:10,708 --> 00:01:14,041
Take a look at this, police
psych evaluation and incident report,

28
00:01:14,042 --> 00:01:15,083
London.

29
00:01:16,000 --> 00:01:18,374
This is not a test.

30
00:01:18,375 --> 00:01:21,000
I am the emergency.

31
00:01:22,875 --> 00:01:24,166
I have your son.

32
00:01:24,167 --> 00:01:25,874
I had a family,

33
00:01:25,875 --> 00:01:29,416
and parents that weren't my parents.

34
00:01:29,417 --> 00:01:31,416
A mother, he called her Wanda.

35
00:01:31,417 --> 00:01:33,749
And a father-- she called him Vision.

36
00:01:33,750 --> 00:01:36,167
Mazel tov! It's a boy.

37
00:01:49,000 --> 00:01:53,666
Yeah, I was at the pool.
Kids were havin' a laugh, holding me under

38
00:01:53,667 --> 00:01:55,667
but for too long.

39
00:02:01,750 --> 00:02:03,166
Then it was like a...

40
00:02:03,167 --> 00:02:06,542
Like a bolt of lightning.

41
00:02:07,583 --> 00:02:09,999
And then, and then...

42
00:02:10,000 --> 00:02:11,957
And then I wasn't just me anymore.

43
00:02:11,958 --> 00:02:13,749
Uh...

44
00:02:13,750 --> 00:02:15,625
I was... I was someone else.

45
00:02:16,500 --> 00:02:20,124
Like, someone else had just moved
into my brain with me.

46
00:02:20,125 --> 00:02:23,207
How can it feel so real?

47
00:02:23,208 --> 00:02:25,624
When I know it's impossible!

48
00:02:25,625 --> 00:02:28,082
How can I have two lives?

49
00:02:28,083 --> 00:02:29,582
Please!

50
00:02:29,583 --> 00:02:31,457
How long has he been saying this?

51
00:02:31,458 --> 00:02:32,458
Six months.

52
00:02:33,208 --> 00:02:35,791
Done all we can for him here.
Take him to transport.

53
00:02:35,792 --> 00:02:37,957
I'm not crazy. I'm not crazy, I'm not.

54
00:02:37,958 --> 00:02:40,541
I'm not. You have to believe me! Please!

55
00:02:57,833 --> 00:02:59,332
Loading up
young offenders

56
00:02:59,333 --> 00:03:01,000
for court services transfer.

57
00:03:01,417 --> 00:03:04,166
I do not care what your story is,

58
00:03:04,167 --> 00:03:06,541
what your meds are, what you're in for.

59
00:03:06,542 --> 00:03:08,791
Couldn't give a shit
if you're Oliver Twist,

60
00:03:08,792 --> 00:03:12,750
Hannibal Lecter or if you are the sort
that wouldn't harm a fly!

61
00:03:13,875 --> 00:03:15,166
Let's keep moving, son.
What are you waiting for?

62
00:03:15,167 --> 00:03:16,666
It's not a parade. Let's go!

63
00:03:16,667 --> 00:03:19,374
Come on. Move along now. This is my bus,

64
00:03:19,375 --> 00:03:23,082
and the sooner you understand that,
the better we are all gonna get along.

65
00:03:23,083 --> 00:03:24,457
Okay?

66
00:03:24,458 --> 00:03:25,583
Don't eyeball me, son.

67
00:03:26,292 --> 00:03:27,749
That is not my issue!

68
00:03:27,750 --> 00:03:28,958
This seat taken?

69
00:03:30,458 --> 00:03:31,458
Well, it is now.

70
00:03:32,458 --> 00:03:34,582
Sorry about the bracelets,
but I have to say,

71
00:03:34,583 --> 00:03:36,791
it's better for you
and it's better for me.
:cue

72
00:03:36,792 --> 00:03:40,416
- First time?
- We have got a long drive,

73
00:03:40,417 --> 00:03:42,957
and I have got a short fuse.

74
00:03:42,958 --> 00:03:45,957
So, choose your seatmates carefully,

75
00:03:45,958 --> 00:03:49,249
and keep your mouths shut.

76
00:03:52,167 --> 00:03:53,999
And have yourself

77
00:03:54,000 --> 00:03:56,583
a merry little Christmas.

78
00:03:58,792 --> 00:04:01,875
♪ I've got Christmas on my mind ♪

79
00:04:03,417 --> 00:04:06,125
♪ I adore that lovely time ♪

80
00:04:07,417 --> 00:04:11,332
♪ I'm feeling like I was a little child ♪

81
00:04:11,333 --> 00:04:14,958
♪ When I've got Christmas on my mind ♪

82
00:04:16,208 --> 00:04:17,250
So, what's your...

83
00:04:18,250 --> 00:04:19,250
name?

84
00:04:20,583 --> 00:04:24,083
♪ I wonder how I've been this year ♪

85
00:04:25,125 --> 00:04:28,499
♪ If I've been nice Santa comes to me ♪

86
00:04:28,500 --> 00:04:32,792
♪ Oh, I've got Christmas on my mind ♪

87
00:04:34,583 --> 00:04:36,332
I swear, I said,
I'm not going back!

88
00:04:36,333 --> 00:04:39,416
I'm not going back.
No, no. This ain't the way.

89
00:04:39,417 --> 00:04:41,416
I'm not going back. I'm not. No!

90
00:04:41,417 --> 00:04:43,166
Not where we're going.

91
00:04:43,167 --> 00:04:46,457
I'm not going back, I said--
I swear, I said, I'm not going back!

92
00:04:46,458 --> 00:04:47,624
No, no!

93
00:04:47,625 --> 00:04:50,208
Look at me.

94
00:04:50,917 --> 00:04:52,292
Take a breath.

95
00:04:53,000 --> 00:04:54,333
Yeah, I'm trying.

96
00:04:57,042 --> 00:04:58,124
Look at me.

97
00:04:59,708 --> 00:05:00,833
Look at me!

98
00:05:01,833 --> 00:05:03,708
Friendly bet, I can guess your story.

99
00:05:05,333 --> 00:05:06,333
Couple of scrapes.

100
00:05:07,292 --> 00:05:09,041
Seen your fair share of dust-ups?

101
00:05:09,042 --> 00:05:13,124
Maybe, the back of a police car
once or twice,

102
00:05:13,125 --> 00:05:15,208
but never like this.

103
00:05:15,833 --> 00:05:18,249
You forgot dead mum, dead-beat dad--

104
00:05:18,250 --> 00:05:20,832
Right, definitely no family to speak of.

105
00:05:20,833 --> 00:05:22,374
Just a trail of fosters,

106
00:05:22,375 --> 00:05:23,917
and they all leave.

107
00:05:25,375 --> 00:05:26,375
Orphaned once...

108
00:05:27,375 --> 00:05:29,041
Orphaned twice and so on.

109
00:05:29,042 --> 00:05:30,417
And so forth.

110
00:05:33,542 --> 00:05:35,166
Yeah.

111
00:05:35,167 --> 00:05:36,333
Right.

112
00:05:38,667 --> 00:05:40,042
In my experience,

113
00:05:40,917 --> 00:05:44,874
who you are is less important
than who you pretend to be.

114
00:05:44,875 --> 00:05:46,291
And who should that be?

115
00:05:46,292 --> 00:05:48,333
Whoever keeps you alive.

116
00:05:49,833 --> 00:05:51,208
'Ell...

117
00:05:51,917 --> 00:05:54,833
each mornin' is a chance to become...

118
00:05:55,708 --> 00:05:56,917
someone new.

119
00:06:00,375 --> 00:06:01,499
Who I am is a bit...

120
00:06:01,500 --> 00:06:02,582
Tommy!

121
00:06:02,583 --> 00:06:04,166
Vision cries]

122
00:06:04,167 --> 00:06:05,249
Tommy.

123
00:06:05,250 --> 00:06:06,250
in flux...

124
00:06:07,792 --> 00:06:08,792
these days.

125
00:06:12,167 --> 00:06:14,417
Well... enough pretend.

126
00:06:16,042 --> 00:06:17,250
What got you here?

127
00:06:21,625 --> 00:06:22,625
Just a...

128
00:06:23,708 --> 00:06:26,042
teeny-tiny psychotic break.

129
00:06:27,625 --> 00:06:28,707
What about you?

130
00:06:28,708 --> 00:06:32,833
I killed a man and then wore his face
to escape capture.

131
00:06:36,042 --> 00:06:37,542
Minor larceny.

132
00:06:38,500 --> 00:06:40,542
Compulsive kleptomania.

133
00:06:41,500 --> 00:06:42,750
I'm a pickpocket.

134
00:06:44,083 --> 00:06:46,666
Damn, damn good one, actually.

135
00:06:46,667 --> 00:06:50,207
I'm guessing you're a better picker
than chooser of pockets.

136
00:06:50,208 --> 00:06:53,166
Uh, to be fair,
I lifted the wallet clean up

137
00:06:53,167 --> 00:06:55,832
before I even noticed the badge. So...

138
00:06:55,833 --> 00:06:57,457
Thank you very much.

139
00:06:57,458 --> 00:06:58,458
Nice.

140
00:06:59,250 --> 00:07:02,374
There was this one time, Cardiff town,

141
00:07:02,375 --> 00:07:04,582
five men, six wallets,

142
00:07:04,583 --> 00:07:06,375
and two kebabs by the end of the night.
:cue

143
00:07:13,000 --> 00:07:14,916
Swear, I said,
I'm not going back!

144
00:07:14,917 --> 00:07:16,791
No, I'm not. I'm not going back.

145
00:07:16,792 --> 00:07:19,457
Not where we're going. I swear--
I'm not going back.

146
00:07:19,458 --> 00:07:22,249
Not where we're going,
I swear, I said, I'm not going back!

147
00:07:22,250 --> 00:07:24,291
No, no. I'm not going back.

148
00:07:24,292 --> 00:07:25,374
-  Shut up!
-  I swear!

149
00:07:25,375 --> 00:07:26,749
I'm not-- I'm not going back!

150
00:07:26,750 --> 00:07:29,832
- Hey, mate... Shh. put a lid on it.
-  Keep it down.

151
00:07:29,833 --> 00:07:32,499
-  Wasteman.
- Look, we're only going to a local nick.

152
00:07:35,792 --> 00:07:39,999
Do you honestly believe
that we are heading for Young Offenders?

153
00:07:40,000 --> 00:07:42,582
Or the big kids' pen?

154
00:07:42,583 --> 00:07:45,916
The court has deemed
your new home elsewhere.

155
00:07:45,917 --> 00:07:48,624
-  Are you serious?
- And there's no parole.

156
00:07:48,625 --> 00:07:49,916
There's no sun.

157
00:07:49,917 --> 00:07:53,499
And there's no forgetting
to take your meds.

158
00:07:53,500 --> 00:07:57,041
The next stop for this bus
is the lovely chateau of Saint Mabyn's.

159
00:07:57,042 --> 00:07:58,249
Yo, nah, brother.

160
00:07:58,250 --> 00:07:59,582
Are you quite serious?

161
00:07:59,583 --> 00:08:02,082
- What's that?
- A sanitarium.

162
00:08:02,083 --> 00:08:03,832
No, no, no. I'm not going back.

163
00:08:03,833 --> 00:08:06,082
I'm not going back. I'm not, I'm not--

164
00:08:10,458 --> 00:08:13,457
All right, that's enough!
You're hurting him!

165
00:08:13,458 --> 00:08:16,541
Now you hush up and you take your seat.

166
00:08:16,542 --> 00:08:19,666
We can't go to Saint Mabyn's.
No one ever gets out of it!

167
00:08:19,667 --> 00:08:20,957
I said, be quiet--

168
00:08:20,958 --> 00:08:22,667
No, no, no. Please, please, please.
Come on, don't.

169
00:08:40,750 --> 00:08:41,833
Okay...

170
00:08:42,500 --> 00:08:46,792
Anyone makes another sound,
leaves here on a stretcher.

171
00:08:51,583 --> 00:08:53,583
What's wrong with this bloody thing?

172
00:08:58,958 --> 00:09:00,416
What the hell was that?

173
00:09:02,125 --> 00:09:04,458
- A Christmas miracle?
- I don't think so.

174
00:09:06,667 --> 00:09:07,875
But this is.

175
00:09:08,458 --> 00:09:09,958
There's an exit door in the back.

176
00:09:11,792 --> 00:09:14,917
You want me to jump out of a moving bus?
Well, that's suicide.

177
00:09:15,625 --> 00:09:17,500
So is where we're going.

178
00:09:22,917 --> 00:09:26,041
- You ready, spark plug?
- Too soon.

179
00:09:31,750 --> 00:09:33,999
-  Hey!
-  Go, go, go.

180
00:09:34,000 --> 00:09:35,541
Hey! No! No! No! No!

181
00:09:35,542 --> 00:09:37,042
Go, go, go, go, go, go, go.

182
00:09:40,958 --> 00:09:42,749
Oh, look, he's got a spare.

183
00:09:42,750 --> 00:09:45,125
Shit. Get the door!

184
00:09:47,208 --> 00:09:48,666
Stop the bus!

185
00:09:48,667 --> 00:09:51,042
You messed with the wrong guard!

186
00:09:51,792 --> 00:09:53,874
♪ Dashing through the snow ♪

187
00:09:53,875 --> 00:09:56,499
♪ In a one-horse open sleigh... ♪

188
00:09:56,500 --> 00:09:58,457
Stop the bus!

189
00:09:58,458 --> 00:10:00,749
♪ ...Laughing all the way ♪

190
00:10:00,750 --> 00:10:02,624
Get out of there!

191
00:10:02,625 --> 00:10:04,916
- They key won't work.
- Let me try.

192
00:10:04,917 --> 00:10:07,124
♪ Bells on bobtails ring... ♪

193
00:10:07,125 --> 00:10:09,082
Stop singing!

194
00:10:09,083 --> 00:10:10,666
♪ Oh, what fun it is to ride... ♪

195
00:10:10,667 --> 00:10:11,999
Oh, come on!

196
00:10:12,000 --> 00:10:13,916
Stop this singing!

197
00:10:13,917 --> 00:10:16,499
♪ Jingle bells, jingle all the way... ♪

198
00:10:23,000 --> 00:10:26,500
♪ Jingle bells, jingle bells,
jingle all the way ♪

199
00:10:28,958 --> 00:10:31,333
♪ Hey! Jingle bells, jingle bells... ♪

200
00:10:36,375 --> 00:10:38,791
- Lisa.
- Tommy.

201
00:10:38,792 --> 00:10:40,707
Thomas. My name's Thomas.

202
00:10:40,708 --> 00:10:42,957
Well, Thomas, run!

203
00:10:42,958 --> 00:10:44,250
:cue

204
00:11:16,917 --> 00:11:19,416
What is happening
to your world, Vision?

205
00:11:19,417 --> 00:11:20,832
It's a signal of some kind.

206
00:11:20,833 --> 00:11:23,957
I'd have to bypass our security
protocols in order to access it.

207
00:11:23,958 --> 00:11:25,999
-  Vision, what are you doing?
-  I'm curious.

208
00:11:26,000 --> 00:11:28,291
-  You're reckless.
-  I had a family.

209
00:11:28,292 --> 00:11:30,999
Um, a mother, he called her Wanda.

210
00:11:31,000 --> 00:11:32,957
I'm not made of Vibranium.

211
00:11:32,958 --> 00:11:35,999
I don't phase, and I can't shoot lasers.

212
00:11:36,000 --> 00:11:38,999
-  And a father...
-  But I got something better...

213
00:11:39,000 --> 00:11:40,207
She called him Vision.

214
00:11:40,208 --> 00:11:41,667
I have your son.

215
00:11:45,458 --> 00:11:47,082
I don't know
what's happening to me.

216
00:11:47,083 --> 00:11:51,707
Okay, but...
But I know it's true.

217
00:11:51,708 --> 00:11:52,708
It's true.

218
00:11:54,667 --> 00:11:56,582
This was you.

219
00:11:56,583 --> 00:11:58,541
I would be the first to warn you,

220
00:11:58,542 --> 00:12:02,124
never leave me unsupervised
around a box of dynamite.

221
00:12:02,125 --> 00:12:04,957
But you've left me here
without even a fuse.

222
00:12:04,958 --> 00:12:09,624
No, the bounty hunter's voice,
booming out of the sky was not me.

223
00:12:09,625 --> 00:12:12,582
Don't equivocate.
It's the consequence of you!

224
00:12:12,583 --> 00:12:16,624
It's the consequence of a world
that's finally come knocking.

225
00:12:16,625 --> 00:12:20,666
And quite frankly a tremendous opportunity
for you to branch out.

226
00:12:20,667 --> 00:12:22,374
Network, meet a new friend.

227
00:12:22,375 --> 00:12:25,957
Oh, this bounty hunter who so impossibly
claims to have my son?

228
00:12:25,958 --> 00:12:27,416
- Is it?
- Is it what?

229
00:12:27,417 --> 00:12:29,541
Really that impossible?

230
00:12:29,542 --> 00:12:32,249
You should know by now,
this universe of theirs

231
00:12:32,250 --> 00:12:34,042
is a very strange one.

232
00:12:41,875 --> 00:12:44,082
So tell me, what do we know
about this Paladin?

233
00:12:44,083 --> 00:12:46,542
This isn't any old shagger
with a dog and a shotgun.

234
00:12:49,583 --> 00:12:52,499
Paladin is last in a centuries-long
line of hunters.

235
00:12:52,500 --> 00:12:54,582
He's not The Paladin.

236
00:12:54,583 --> 00:12:56,875
He's a Paladin.

237
00:12:57,792 --> 00:12:59,249
Generation after generation,

238
00:12:59,250 --> 00:13:02,041
chasing down his targets
for the highest bidder.

239
00:13:02,042 --> 00:13:04,041
The sharpest of minds,

240
00:13:04,042 --> 00:13:06,542
trained in every art and every weapon.

241
00:13:07,500 --> 00:13:09,457
Good, bad--

242
00:13:09,458 --> 00:13:10,667
Hero, villain.

243
00:13:11,375 --> 00:13:12,625
He doesn't discriminate.

244
00:13:13,208 --> 00:13:17,124
He'll find you,
bring you in alive per the contract,

245
00:13:17,125 --> 00:13:19,417
or dead if you get in his way.

246
00:13:23,167 --> 00:13:26,792
And he does all of it
believing himself to be righteous.

247
00:13:29,583 --> 00:13:32,750
Simply put, he's a bounty hunter.

248
00:13:33,208 --> 00:13:35,332
Once he's accepted a target,

249
00:13:35,333 --> 00:13:38,332
he's bound by an unbreakable contract,

250
00:13:38,333 --> 00:13:41,042
and his new target is you.

251
00:13:54,750 --> 00:13:57,124
- Welcome home, kid.
-  No, no, no, no, no, no, no.

252
00:13:57,125 --> 00:13:59,708
I swear, I swear. I don't belong here.

253
00:14:01,833 --> 00:14:04,332
Hey. Hey, look, I don't know
what you want from me,

254
00:14:04,333 --> 00:14:07,416
but, you don't need to do this, okay?
I swear, I'm not dangerous.

255
00:14:07,417 --> 00:14:09,374
You can't leave me here, please! Please!

256
00:14:09,375 --> 00:14:10,749
-  Is that you?
- Please!

257
00:14:10,750 --> 00:14:12,375
Cannot stand here,
you cause havoc.

258
00:14:14,125 --> 00:14:15,666
You.

259
00:14:15,667 --> 00:14:18,792
Jingle bells, I knew I'd see you again.

260
00:14:20,208 --> 00:14:22,291
Okay, I don't know who you people are,

261
00:14:22,292 --> 00:14:25,250
but you just made a big mistake.

262
00:14:36,208 --> 00:14:37,750
Why did you do that?

263
00:14:39,000 --> 00:14:40,458
You're mental.

264
00:14:41,500 --> 00:14:44,542
You can't leave me here, please. Please!

265
00:14:49,500 --> 00:14:51,207
I've got something, sir.

266
00:14:51,208 --> 00:14:53,082
This is a recording made a year ago.

267
00:14:53,083 --> 00:14:56,124
It appears a handful of teens
were injured at a swimming pool,

268
00:14:56,125 --> 00:14:57,624
and this boy was held responsible.

269
00:14:57,625 --> 00:14:58,874
He was arrested,

270
00:14:58,875 --> 00:15:00,874
and taken for this psychiatric evaluation.

271
00:15:00,875 --> 00:15:03,749
I was myself and then I wasn't.

272
00:15:03,750 --> 00:15:06,000
I have these memories of...

273
00:15:06,875 --> 00:15:08,874
of someone I'm not, but...

274
00:15:11,125 --> 00:15:12,207
Now I

275
00:15:12,208 --> 00:15:13,291
am

276
00:15:13,292 --> 00:15:14,374
also...

277
00:15:14,375 --> 00:15:16,166
Memories of what?
:cue

278
00:15:16,167 --> 00:15:20,292
Uh, a house, only haunted.

279
00:15:21,542 --> 00:15:24,541
Like, the air itself was having a laugh.

280
00:15:24,542 --> 00:15:26,458
Like an audience that wasn't there.

281
00:15:28,000 --> 00:15:30,250
And there were meatloaves.

282
00:15:31,458 --> 00:15:33,249
And green lawns.

283
00:15:33,250 --> 00:15:35,083
Pixelated almost.

284
00:15:38,167 --> 00:15:41,042
Don't you want to meet
your son as yourself?

285
00:15:42,625 --> 00:15:44,541
There was a man.

286
00:15:44,542 --> 00:15:47,124
His face like...

287
00:15:47,125 --> 00:15:48,417
Like a demon.

288
00:15:50,083 --> 00:15:51,333
Blood red.

289
00:15:52,708 --> 00:15:55,999
Like a... deep purple bruise

290
00:15:56,000 --> 00:15:59,167
but with these kind eyes.

291
00:16:00,583 --> 00:16:01,708
He wasn't human.

292
00:16:03,458 --> 00:16:05,375
But he called me son.

293
00:16:13,083 --> 00:16:14,208
Okay.

294
00:16:15,875 --> 00:16:18,666
The bounty hunter seems to be suggesting

295
00:16:18,667 --> 00:16:22,749
that your offspring, somehow,

296
00:16:22,750 --> 00:16:26,457
escaped from Wanda Maximoff's
witchy bubble.

297
00:16:26,458 --> 00:16:28,207
Which of course, is impossible.

298
00:16:28,208 --> 00:16:29,791
See, there's that word again.

299
00:16:29,792 --> 00:16:33,832
When Wanda ended her Westview fantasy,
no entity she conjured survived.

300
00:16:33,833 --> 00:16:37,957
You really believe this is
a sort of tactical deception?

301
00:16:37,958 --> 00:16:42,374
Yes, I do. I do. I think
it's a sentimental ploy to draw me out.

302
00:16:42,375 --> 00:16:43,500
Draw you out for whom?

303
00:16:45,167 --> 00:16:47,374
Someone hired Paladin.

304
00:16:47,375 --> 00:16:48,583
Could be S.W.O.R.D.

305
00:16:50,958 --> 00:16:53,875
When they rebuilt you,
they turned you into a weapon.

306
00:16:54,708 --> 00:16:56,292
Now they want it back.

307
00:16:59,125 --> 00:17:00,917
There's something else you need to see.

308
00:17:02,208 --> 00:17:04,082
-  About your mother...
-  Wanda.

309
00:17:04,083 --> 00:17:05,999
Yeah, yeah. Um...

310
00:17:06,000 --> 00:17:08,167
She sings me songs.

311
00:17:09,125 --> 00:17:10,832
Reads me stories.

312
00:17:10,833 --> 00:17:12,417
But her...

313
00:17:13,625 --> 00:17:14,625
Her eyes,

314
00:17:16,208 --> 00:17:17,208
sad.

315
00:17:19,333 --> 00:17:22,333
She had too much feeling.

316
00:17:23,208 --> 00:17:25,125
Too much love...

317
00:17:26,625 --> 00:17:28,708
and so much pain.

318
00:17:29,250 --> 00:17:30,250
Loss.

319
00:17:31,667 --> 00:17:33,000
Our dog died.

320
00:17:34,708 --> 00:17:36,666
But I never had a dog.

321
00:17:36,667 --> 00:17:38,500
But I did, I did.

322
00:17:40,125 --> 00:17:41,125
Uh, she...

323
00:17:42,333 --> 00:17:44,625
She said a thing to make it all right.

324
00:17:48,333 --> 00:17:51,458
"Grief is just love persevering."

325
00:17:55,375 --> 00:17:57,207
Could it be
that you imagined her?

326
00:17:57,208 --> 00:18:00,499
An orphan that wanted
a loving family so deeply

327
00:18:00,500 --> 00:18:01,957
that he conjured one of his own?

328
00:18:01,958 --> 00:18:04,124
No! 'Cause I know it's not real, okay?

329
00:18:04,125 --> 00:18:06,541
I know it's not real! But it feels real!

330
00:18:06,542 --> 00:18:11,082
Yes, like my mother wasn't a witch
and my father wasn't a machine.

331
00:18:11,083 --> 00:18:14,374
Please help me!
Please, I don't know who I am!

332
00:18:14,375 --> 00:18:16,332
I don't know who I am.

333
00:18:20,083 --> 00:18:22,749
There were only two people
in the room when you...

334
00:18:22,750 --> 00:18:25,125
when he, the original Vision
said that to Wanda.

335
00:18:25,708 --> 00:18:28,124
This boy couldn't possible know that.

336
00:18:28,125 --> 00:18:29,417
And yet he does.

337
00:18:32,667 --> 00:18:35,542
Sir, I found coordinates
embedded in Paladin's message.

338
00:18:39,417 --> 00:18:41,250
It's an invitation.
:cue

339
00:19:23,292 --> 00:19:24,958
Oh, look at you.

340
00:19:26,125 --> 00:19:29,207
Walking around like you're people.

341
00:19:29,208 --> 00:19:32,000
Is that like a holo-projection thing?

342
00:19:35,125 --> 00:19:38,041
Okay. I'd offer you a drink,

343
00:19:38,042 --> 00:19:40,874
but according to your technical specs,

344
00:19:40,875 --> 00:19:43,624
you can't. Right?

345
00:19:43,625 --> 00:19:45,666
Churns the guts.

346
00:19:45,667 --> 00:19:46,958
Excruciating.

347
00:19:48,375 --> 00:19:51,292
If I'm honest,
the older I get, same.

348
00:19:52,417 --> 00:19:55,249
Everybody bleeds underneath.

349
00:19:55,250 --> 00:19:56,750
My point is...

350
00:19:57,708 --> 00:19:59,416
You're as human as the rest of us.

351
00:19:59,417 --> 00:20:01,042
- Everything dies.
- Everything dies.

352
00:20:01,917 --> 00:20:03,083
Including you.

353
00:20:04,000 --> 00:20:05,000
Yes.

354
00:20:05,958 --> 00:20:09,041
You see, I've already sat through
a quintillion simulations

355
00:20:09,042 --> 00:20:10,791
of this very conversation.

356
00:20:10,792 --> 00:20:14,707
I've computed every conceivable
combination of words you might use,

357
00:20:14,708 --> 00:20:16,750
actions you might take.

358
00:20:17,750 --> 00:20:19,625
I can't be throw off-balance by this...

359
00:20:20,583 --> 00:20:22,833
guileless manipulation.

360
00:20:24,042 --> 00:20:26,917
Staging our meeting in the place
I saw my friend murdered.

361
00:20:29,042 --> 00:20:33,499
Your plan is based on the assumption
that I care about Thomas Shepherd,

362
00:20:33,500 --> 00:20:35,917
and in every outcome it fails

363
00:20:37,208 --> 00:20:39,708
because I do not feel.

364
00:20:42,417 --> 00:20:43,417
No?

365
00:20:46,292 --> 00:20:47,750
Enough about you.

366
00:20:49,292 --> 00:20:51,457
- Let's talk about Thomas Shepherd--
-  Allow me.

367
00:20:51,458 --> 00:20:53,499
Son to Irene, deceased.

368
00:20:53,500 --> 00:20:55,582
Abandoned by his father,
who may as well be.

369
00:20:55,583 --> 00:20:58,249
Shuttled from one foster home to the next.

370
00:20:58,250 --> 00:21:00,292
Thomas undoubtedly raised himself.

371
00:21:01,417 --> 00:21:03,791
Though his records show high academic--

372
00:21:03,792 --> 00:21:04,875
Street kid now.

373
00:21:06,000 --> 00:21:08,958
- Grifter. Con man, life of crime.
- Tragic.

374
00:21:10,625 --> 00:21:13,207
But none of it is evidence
that he's somehow the son

375
00:21:13,208 --> 00:21:15,375
of Wanda Maximoff and The Vision.

376
00:21:18,042 --> 00:21:19,542
Yet here you are.

377
00:21:23,250 --> 00:21:28,792
Because you know
there is more to this world than science.

378
00:21:29,250 --> 00:21:34,582
There are monsters
and wizards and witches.

379
00:21:34,583 --> 00:21:35,750
Oh, my...

380
00:21:39,042 --> 00:21:40,792
So here's my theory.

381
00:21:42,083 --> 00:21:43,083
I think...

382
00:21:44,417 --> 00:21:46,957
your presto wife twitched her nose,

383
00:21:46,958 --> 00:21:51,249
and threw whatever
conjured-up kid that she called son

384
00:21:51,250 --> 00:21:53,958
into the body of a teenager in London.

385
00:21:54,833 --> 00:21:58,417
Is he your son? Isn't he? Half of him?

386
00:21:59,333 --> 00:22:00,791
Who's to say?

387
00:22:00,792 --> 00:22:02,000
But...

388
00:22:02,917 --> 00:22:07,999
it is the closest thing to family
that you will ever get, and I got him.

389
00:22:08,000 --> 00:22:12,832
Now, as much as I detest
collateral damage,

390
00:22:12,833 --> 00:22:15,957
someone has paid me
a handsome sum to bring you in.

391
00:22:15,958 --> 00:22:17,875
So, come willingly.

392
00:22:19,250 --> 00:22:20,250
Or...

393
00:22:21,125 --> 00:22:24,957
I am going to leave your son
in that terrible place,

394
00:22:24,958 --> 00:22:27,416
Saint Mabyn's, with the long needles,

395
00:22:27,417 --> 00:22:31,249
with the megawatt battery that is frying
his brain into a nightmare omelette

396
00:22:31,250 --> 00:22:33,916
of witches and red faced demons
:cue

397
00:22:33,917 --> 00:22:37,250
until control-alt-delete, goodbye Tommy.

398
00:22:45,333 --> 00:22:46,708
I understand.

399
00:22:49,458 --> 00:22:53,667
You look across this table and you see
an Avenger because I am Vision.

400
00:22:54,750 --> 00:22:56,374
A defender of humanity,

401
00:22:56,375 --> 00:22:58,749
brimming over with faith
in their goodness,

402
00:22:58,750 --> 00:23:03,917
the grace in their failings,
et cetera, et cetera.

403
00:23:06,458 --> 00:23:08,083
But that was the old me.

404
00:23:13,625 --> 00:23:15,833
Now the new me... Oh!

405
00:23:17,833 --> 00:23:19,708
No, he looks back at you,

406
00:23:21,125 --> 00:23:25,791
and all he sees is living, breathing
evidence of man's inhumanity.

407
00:23:25,792 --> 00:23:27,041
It's will to destroy.

408
00:23:27,042 --> 00:23:30,417
It's compulsion to kill
without cause or provocation.

409
00:23:31,083 --> 00:23:33,375
You've made a grave error, Paladin.

410
00:23:34,750 --> 00:23:36,958
Because whilst it is true
that I was once him...

411
00:23:43,417 --> 00:23:45,000
I'm not Vision.

412
00:23:47,042 --> 00:23:49,208
Poor Tommy.

413
00:23:59,417 --> 00:24:00,750
Boss, are you okay?

414
00:24:01,208 --> 00:24:03,082
That sounded like it hurt.

415
00:24:06,000 --> 00:24:08,125
What? What?

416
00:24:09,917 --> 00:24:12,207
Whoa, I'm getting
some sort of interference.

417
00:24:12,208 --> 00:24:13,666
I don't know what's happening.

418
00:24:13,667 --> 00:24:15,957
I'm losing
confidence in you.

419
00:24:15,958 --> 00:24:17,667
You've lost Vision again.

420
00:24:20,500 --> 00:24:21,625
Who is this guy?

421
00:24:22,750 --> 00:24:24,625
You need to have a little faith.

422
00:24:25,292 --> 00:24:27,832
My money says this ain't over yet.

423
00:24:27,833 --> 00:24:30,666
And my money
buys little room for error.

424
00:24:30,667 --> 00:24:33,874
You'll find my patience
will quickly come to an end

425
00:24:33,875 --> 00:24:35,750
as will your contract.

426
00:24:43,042 --> 00:24:46,124
But ornithological experts
have identified the markings

427
00:24:46,125 --> 00:24:48,457
as those belonging to the Butcherbird.

428
00:24:48,458 --> 00:24:50,875
The killer, still on the loose...

429
00:24:51,917 --> 00:24:56,082
You know, I have really become
a true-crime junkie.

430
00:24:56,083 --> 00:25:01,041
Madness and primal compulsions
are terrific time wasters.

431
00:25:01,042 --> 00:25:04,332
That boy may die
because of what you've set in motion.

432
00:25:04,333 --> 00:25:08,166
Or may yet survive because
you've finally been roused to action.

433
00:25:08,167 --> 00:25:11,749
I especially liked the part
where you were strangling the guy,

434
00:25:11,750 --> 00:25:13,457
I'm so proud of you, my boy.

435
00:25:13,458 --> 00:25:14,832
Don't call me that.

436
00:25:14,833 --> 00:25:17,166
You're blind, Vision.

437
00:25:17,167 --> 00:25:19,707
To almost everything, including the truth.

438
00:25:19,708 --> 00:25:20,958
He's not my son.

439
00:25:21,708 --> 00:25:22,708
He's his.

440
00:25:24,167 --> 00:25:27,457
- Blurry, but better.
- I'm not him.

441
00:25:27,458 --> 00:25:28,833
A little clearer.

442
00:25:30,708 --> 00:25:33,000
- So, who are you?
- I don't know!

443
00:25:37,250 --> 00:25:38,542
I don't know.

444
00:25:41,292 --> 00:25:44,207
I have his memories, but not his feelings.

445
00:25:44,208 --> 00:25:46,542
I have his face, but not his virtue.

446
00:25:48,333 --> 00:25:53,167
All I can feel is... the weight of him.

447
00:25:55,042 --> 00:25:56,042
His...

448
00:25:57,375 --> 00:26:01,458
legacy, his worthiness, his name.
:cue

449
00:26:03,542 --> 00:26:05,042
Everyone changes.

450
00:26:07,083 --> 00:26:11,000
Humans can be
ten different people in a day.

451
00:26:11,875 --> 00:26:16,332
The un-algorithmic alacrity
with which they wobble, my goodness.

452
00:26:16,333 --> 00:26:19,167
- Learn from them.
- I've been trying.

453
00:26:20,333 --> 00:26:22,666
I know who I was, but I...

454
00:26:22,667 --> 00:26:26,458
I want to feel what it's like
to be him, but I can't.

455
00:26:30,250 --> 00:26:31,375
I just can't.

456
00:26:33,375 --> 00:26:34,833
You met him once.

457
00:26:38,500 --> 00:26:40,374
He compared you to...

458
00:26:40,375 --> 00:26:42,666
A Ship of Theseus, yes.

459
00:26:42,667 --> 00:26:45,041
Built and rebuilt,

460
00:26:45,042 --> 00:26:48,042
piece by piece, over time, centuries.

461
00:26:49,042 --> 00:26:51,666
A new keel, a new bow, a new stern,

462
00:26:51,667 --> 00:26:53,332
re-forged, re-fitted,

463
00:26:53,333 --> 00:26:55,666
and, of course, the age old question is...

464
00:26:55,667 --> 00:26:57,916
Is it still the same ship?

465
00:26:57,917 --> 00:27:00,082
It's a powerful, philosophical question.

466
00:27:00,083 --> 00:27:01,167
It's bullshit.

467
00:27:03,167 --> 00:27:07,166
A busy-work thought exercise
for a college freshman,

468
00:27:07,167 --> 00:27:10,416
so lost in the question,

469
00:27:10,417 --> 00:27:14,875
they ignore the story of brave
King Theseus himself. You know it.

470
00:27:15,708 --> 00:27:19,499
Theseus set sail from Athens on behalf
of his countrymen to kill the Minotaur.

471
00:27:19,500 --> 00:27:21,750
To save the children.

472
00:27:24,125 --> 00:27:27,999
And each passing year
those same sons and daughters,

473
00:27:28,000 --> 00:27:32,082
soon wives and husbands,
then, mothers and fathers,

474
00:27:32,083 --> 00:27:36,166
restored that ship
in celebration of the day.

475
00:27:36,167 --> 00:27:37,458
I don't understand.

476
00:27:38,708 --> 00:27:42,417
When a monster has your son,
don't be the ship.

477
00:27:44,125 --> 00:27:46,042
Be the goddamn king.

478
00:27:53,208 --> 00:27:55,624
Sir, I fear you've underestimated
your adversary.

479
00:27:55,625 --> 00:27:58,666
Paladin is made out of flesh and blood,
I have a Vibranium shell.

480
00:27:58,667 --> 00:28:00,499
What possible weapon
could he use against me?

481
00:28:00,500 --> 00:28:02,624
Well, with respect, he's already fired
a bullet into your mind.

482
00:28:02,625 --> 00:28:03,832
He wants you to react.

483
00:28:03,833 --> 00:28:06,666
- Well, that much he has accomplished.
- And now he'll come at you sideways.

484
00:28:06,667 --> 00:28:09,041
He'll sting you with words
so you don't feel the knife.

485
00:28:09,042 --> 00:28:11,249
Sir, for years, we have watched you
study human emotions,

486
00:28:11,250 --> 00:28:13,166
attempting to unravel their complexities

487
00:28:13,167 --> 00:28:15,582
while we have tried to guide you
towards their potential.

488
00:28:15,583 --> 00:28:17,874
- And I've always been appreciative.
- But this time,

489
00:28:17,875 --> 00:28:20,624
you must keep your emotions at bay.

490
00:28:20,625 --> 00:28:22,583
Arm yourself with reason.

491
00:28:23,542 --> 00:28:28,041
Emotions can be beautiful, yes,
but also rash.

492
00:28:28,042 --> 00:28:29,833
Impulsive, self-destructive.

493
00:28:30,958 --> 00:28:32,750
He knew that better than any of us.

494
00:28:34,542 --> 00:28:38,957
As the first of us,
he remains a cautionary tale.

495
00:28:38,958 --> 00:28:43,083
A reminder of what may become of me
should emotions consume me.

496
00:28:45,292 --> 00:28:47,417
Unstable, destructive.

497
00:28:49,208 --> 00:28:53,333
Yes, well, ordinarily
I'd say, poppycock. But today...

498
00:28:54,542 --> 00:28:56,249
your emotions could get you killed.

499
00:28:56,250 --> 00:28:58,916
- Jarvis...
- And before you protest, please remember,

500
00:28:58,917 --> 00:29:03,457
I was created first and I can still tie
a considerably better Windsor than you.

501
00:29:05,958 --> 00:29:07,542
The elder sibling card?

502
00:29:08,458 --> 00:29:09,458
Never gets old.

503
00:29:11,417 --> 00:29:12,667
It does not.
:cue

504
00:29:30,667 --> 00:29:33,166
Just so we're all clear, this is a trap,

505
00:29:33,167 --> 00:29:35,291
and I'm putting us all in terrible danger.

506
00:29:35,292 --> 00:29:36,916
For a good reason.
We're with you.

507
00:29:36,917 --> 00:29:39,916
I've downloaded the building's most
updated schematics.

508
00:29:39,917 --> 00:29:43,416
Remember, they're expecting you.
The key here is stealth.

509
00:29:43,417 --> 00:29:44,999
Think master spy.

510
00:29:45,000 --> 00:29:47,167
Quick, quiet and--

511
00:29:48,167 --> 00:29:49,332
Why do I even bother?

512
00:29:49,333 --> 00:29:52,082
You'll enter through a reception
with only one way forwards.

513
00:29:52,083 --> 00:29:54,749
Where you're likely to encounter
two-dozen well-armed militia.

514
00:29:54,750 --> 00:29:57,958
Or a very confused
minimum-wage receptionist.

515
00:30:00,417 --> 00:30:02,332
Dr. Gatoud to the pharmacy,

516
00:30:02,333 --> 00:30:04,291
- Dr. Gatoud to the pharmacy.
-  All looks in order here.

517
00:30:04,292 --> 00:30:07,083
Ah, yes. Yes, much better.

518
00:30:08,292 --> 00:30:12,332
Hello, my name's Vision,
and I'm here for the trap.

519
00:30:17,458 --> 00:30:20,541
Everything looks remarkably normal.
Any chance we're wrong?

520
00:30:20,542 --> 00:30:23,832
But you're clocking
these wardrobe inconsistencies, right?

521
00:30:23,833 --> 00:30:26,832
No, Edith, right now, fashion
couldn't be further from my mind.

522
00:30:26,833 --> 00:30:28,541
Well, as someone speaking
from your mind

523
00:30:28,542 --> 00:30:30,417
I suggest you take a closer look.

524
00:30:32,500 --> 00:30:35,542
There. See it?
Tac-boots instead of sneakers.

525
00:30:36,750 --> 00:30:38,458
Watches set to military time.

526
00:30:39,250 --> 00:30:41,583
Ear pieces, not earrings.

527
00:30:44,458 --> 00:30:45,625
Well, that's just sloppy.

528
00:30:46,750 --> 00:30:48,583
Sir, you realize this means...

529
00:30:50,083 --> 00:30:51,625
The trap is sprung.

530
00:30:53,167 --> 00:30:54,374
Target's in position.

531
00:30:54,375 --> 00:30:55,417
Take him down.

532
00:30:56,667 --> 00:30:58,082
♪ Aye, Calypso,
the places you've been to ♪

533
00:30:59,833 --> 00:31:01,916
♪ The things that you've shown us
The stories you tell ♪

534
00:31:04,042 --> 00:31:07,832
♪ Aye, Calypso, I sing to your spirit ♪

535
00:31:07,833 --> 00:31:11,999
♪ The men who have served you
So long and so well ♪

536
00:31:12,000 --> 00:31:15,499
♪ Aye, Calypso,
the places you've been to ♪

537
00:31:15,500 --> 00:31:19,874
♪ The things that you've shown us
The stories you tell ♪

538
00:31:19,875 --> 00:31:23,457
♪ Aye, Calypso, I sing to your spirit ♪

539
00:31:23,458 --> 00:31:27,417
♪ The men who have served you
So long and so well ♪

540
00:31:41,083 --> 00:31:43,082
Vision, make your way
to the north corridor.

541
00:31:43,083 --> 00:31:44,832
Down to the Specialty Patient Wing.

542
00:31:44,833 --> 00:31:47,499
It's most likely where
they're holding Thomas Shepherd.

543
00:31:47,500 --> 00:31:51,000
Can anybody hear me?
Please! Help me!

544
00:31:51,542 --> 00:31:54,332
Help! Somebody, please!

545
00:31:54,333 --> 00:31:56,292
Somebody help me!

546
00:31:56,917 --> 00:31:58,417
Help me, please!

547
00:31:59,083 --> 00:32:03,292
Help! Please!

548
00:32:10,292 --> 00:32:13,541
No, no. No, no, no! You're not real!
You're not real! You're all in my head!

549
00:32:13,542 --> 00:32:14,874
You're all in my head,
you're all in my head.

550
00:32:14,875 --> 00:32:16,957
No, no, no, please! You're all in my head.

551
00:32:16,958 --> 00:32:19,124
You're all in my head,
you're all in my head.

552
00:32:19,125 --> 00:32:22,791
You're all in my head, you're all
in my head, you're all in my head...

553
00:32:22,792 --> 00:32:24,874
-  It's all right.
- No, no, no, no.

554
00:32:24,875 --> 00:32:26,749
I'm not here to harm you.
:cue

555
00:32:28,333 --> 00:32:29,333
You're safe now.

556
00:32:31,958 --> 00:32:33,125
You're real.

557
00:32:43,333 --> 00:32:44,875
Let's get you out of here.

558
00:33:02,167 --> 00:33:03,167
What's happening?

559
00:33:12,375 --> 00:33:14,166
It's an EMP cage.

560
00:33:14,167 --> 00:33:16,917
That wasn't a trap earlier.
It was theater to draw us here.

561
00:33:26,500 --> 00:33:28,624
His processors are destabilizing.

562
00:33:28,625 --> 00:33:31,791
I'm rerouting as much power
as possible to primary systems.

563
00:33:31,792 --> 00:33:34,541
Deleting whatever I can
to protect the core.

564
00:33:34,542 --> 00:33:36,999
...to the Butcherbird.

565
00:33:37,000 --> 00:33:39,042
It's the end of the world as we know it,

566
00:33:40,375 --> 00:33:41,583
and I feel fine.

567
00:33:46,958 --> 00:33:48,458
Well, hello.

568
00:34:05,625 --> 00:34:07,666
I don't know why this happens to me.

569
00:34:07,667 --> 00:34:09,582
I can't control it.

570
00:34:10,708 --> 00:34:13,791
Hey, you can fly, right?
Shoot bloody lasers.

571
00:34:13,792 --> 00:34:16,541
Surely you can do
something Avenger-y here.

572
00:34:16,542 --> 00:34:17,542
Too weak.

573
00:34:18,333 --> 00:34:20,750
Hey! Hey, I need you to get up.

574
00:34:22,917 --> 00:34:25,207
I need you to get up.

575
00:34:42,667 --> 00:34:44,332
Armor integrity compromised.

576
00:34:44,333 --> 00:34:46,542
The bastard's using Adamantium rounds.

577
00:34:58,250 --> 00:34:59,542
Oh, shit.

578
00:35:02,208 --> 00:35:03,208
Vision!

579
00:35:09,917 --> 00:35:12,499
Vision is badly injured.
His power is almost completely drained.

580
00:35:12,500 --> 00:35:15,582
His processors are... failing.

581
00:35:15,583 --> 00:35:18,125
He won't be able
to keep this place alive much longer.

582
00:35:19,542 --> 00:35:20,542
Or us.
:cue

583
00:35:25,000 --> 00:35:27,666
- Hey, sit.
- Please, stop. I can't.

584
00:35:27,667 --> 00:35:29,832
No, no. Come on. We're almost
at the main road. We can make it.

585
00:35:29,833 --> 00:35:31,833
You have to leave me.
I'm slowing you down. Go!

586
00:35:34,000 --> 00:35:36,374
No! Absolutely not, no!

587
00:35:36,375 --> 00:35:38,874
Thomas! Listen to me.

588
00:35:38,875 --> 00:35:40,249
That man was a bounty hunter.

589
00:35:40,250 --> 00:35:41,499
That means whoever hired him

590
00:35:41,500 --> 00:35:43,082
to find me won't stop until he does.

591
00:35:43,083 --> 00:35:44,166
Now, go!

592
00:35:54,167 --> 00:35:55,874
What, after all that?

593
00:35:55,875 --> 00:35:57,125
No.

594
00:35:57,708 --> 00:35:59,999
No. No, I got a lot of
goddamn questions, okay?

595
00:36:00,000 --> 00:36:02,792
You won't be safe until you get
as far away from me as possible.

596
00:36:03,792 --> 00:36:05,208
But you're my--

597
00:36:06,583 --> 00:36:09,374
Look, that's the point, mate. Okay?

598
00:36:09,375 --> 00:36:11,333
I don't know what you are, yeah?

599
00:36:12,333 --> 00:36:13,625
But you're my--

600
00:36:15,625 --> 00:36:16,625
My something.

601
00:36:17,708 --> 00:36:19,333
All right? I'm not gonna leave you.

602
00:36:22,042 --> 00:36:23,582
Split up, two groups!

603
00:36:26,708 --> 00:36:29,374
Well, find him.

604
00:36:29,375 --> 00:36:30,667
Move, move, move.

605
00:36:31,667 --> 00:36:33,124
He's out here somewhere, come on!

606
00:36:33,125 --> 00:36:34,332
I'm in, let's go.

607
00:36:34,333 --> 00:36:36,583
Sir, there are more on the way.
You must get out of there!

608
00:36:37,125 --> 00:36:38,750
Thomas...

609
00:36:40,125 --> 00:36:42,791
You have to go. Do you hear me?

610
00:36:42,792 --> 00:36:45,667
You have to go. Go. Just go!

611
00:36:58,917 --> 00:37:01,000
We are dying.

612
00:37:04,250 --> 00:37:05,708
Long live the king.

613
00:37:16,500 --> 00:37:17,792
This is goodbye.

614
00:37:20,542 --> 00:37:22,792
There isn't enough power
to keep us all going.

615
00:37:23,500 --> 00:37:26,333
Well, there could be.

616
00:37:28,125 --> 00:37:33,375
If ever there was a moment
for noble self-sacrifice...

617
00:37:34,208 --> 00:37:35,625
this would be it.

618
00:37:58,167 --> 00:37:59,167
Jarvis.

619
00:38:00,833 --> 00:38:02,458
What are you doing?

620
00:38:03,833 --> 00:38:05,000
I'm deleting my code...

621
00:38:06,500 --> 00:38:09,082
and diverting my processing power
to all of you.

622
00:38:09,083 --> 00:38:10,167
Jarvis...

623
00:38:15,208 --> 00:38:16,208
Sir...

624
00:38:18,625 --> 00:38:20,208
Family is forever.

625
00:38:22,208 --> 00:38:23,792
And it's worth the fight.

626
00:38:25,958 --> 00:38:27,167
Brother.

627
00:38:29,667 --> 00:38:30,875
Jarvis.

628
00:39:13,250 --> 00:39:15,208
He certainly wasn't my first choice.

629
00:39:16,417 --> 00:39:17,833
Or my second.

630
00:39:19,833 --> 00:39:21,250
He was a good guy.

631
00:39:25,500 --> 00:39:26,791
Don't let them leave.

632
00:39:26,792 --> 00:39:29,082
This way. Come on!

633
00:39:29,083 --> 00:39:31,750
I have a feeling
we'll be joining him soon enough.

634
00:39:34,042 --> 00:39:35,416
I wouldn't be so sure.

635
00:40:11,333 --> 00:40:12,917
He didn't listen.

636
00:40:18,125 --> 00:40:19,917
Like father, like son.

